1
00:00:47,672 --> 00:00:50,967
THE APARTMENT JOB

2
00:00:52,051 --> 00:00:53,970
I happened to be there

3
00:00:55,221 --> 00:00:57,640
in his final moments.

4
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:02,227
Why did you do it?

5
00:01:02,228 --> 00:01:04,647
You should have been there for him

6
00:01:05,315 --> 00:01:07,609
when he passed away.

7
00:01:09,194 --> 00:01:11,279
But don't worry.

8
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,616
He didn't suffer when he passed.

9
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:17,160
You…

10
00:01:21,039 --> 00:01:22,332
What did you do?

11
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:27,045
Huh?

12
00:01:32,383 --> 00:01:33,927
Remember how I said

13
00:01:34,511 --> 00:01:36,846
hangnails should be ripped off,
even if you bleed?

14
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:40,766
He seemed to be a hangnail

15
00:01:40,767 --> 00:01:43,478
in your life.

16
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:47,690
So I ripped it off for you.

17
00:01:48,983 --> 00:01:50,819
Don't you feel relieved now?

18
00:01:56,366 --> 00:01:58,451
I offer my deepest

19
00:01:59,911 --> 00:02:01,204
condolences.

20
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:14,968
Well then…

21
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:45,540
Mr. Kim!

22
00:02:46,082 --> 00:02:48,001
Don't make a scene and come here.

23
00:02:49,919 --> 00:02:51,880
You're not some thug.

24
00:02:55,341 --> 00:02:57,760
The chief mourner shouldn't step out.

25
00:02:58,344 --> 00:03:00,054
You should keep your old boss company.

26
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:05,768
You're the hangnail in my life.

27
00:03:06,603 --> 00:03:08,438
I'll rip you off myself,

28
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:12,025
whether I bleed
or tear my own flesh as well.

29
00:03:12,984 --> 00:03:14,193
I'll make sure

30
00:03:15,278 --> 00:03:17,155
you feel the pain.

31
00:03:18,239 --> 00:03:19,949
I'll look forward to it.

32
00:03:21,034 --> 00:03:24,913
But be careful not to rip
your whole nail off.

33
00:03:25,496 --> 00:03:26,788
That pain

34
00:03:26,789 --> 00:03:29,042
will last forever.

35
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:10,749
Move.

36
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:11,876
Where are you going?

37
00:04:13,211 --> 00:04:15,046
Will you go and kill Lee Chung-won?

38
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:17,423
Yong-man just died.

39
00:04:18,758 --> 00:04:21,427
He died because of me.

40
00:04:22,512 --> 00:04:25,515
And you expect me to just stay here,
bowing to him?

41
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:32,521
You're not going to seek revenge.

42
00:04:32,522 --> 00:04:34,399
You're running away from guilt.

43
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:38,528
What?

44
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:40,530
Mr. Park.

45
00:04:41,447 --> 00:04:43,949
You don't even have the guts
to look at his photo.

46
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:46,493
You're a coward running away
by using revenge as an excuse.

47
00:04:46,494 --> 00:04:47,704
Isn't that right?

48
00:04:48,454 --> 00:04:49,788
Going out there and dying

49
00:04:49,789 --> 00:04:51,916
is less scary
than staying here and crying,

50
00:04:52,667 --> 00:04:53,584
isn't it?

51
00:04:56,796 --> 00:04:59,632
What the hell do you know
about how I feel?

52
00:05:00,591 --> 00:05:03,469
I feel like my heart's going to burst!

53
00:05:04,262 --> 00:05:06,097
What am I supposed to do?

54
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:08,516
What should I do, then?

55
00:05:16,774 --> 00:05:18,401
Just cry, Mr. Park.

56
00:05:19,736 --> 00:05:22,405
If you have the guts to die,
just stay here and cry,

57
00:05:23,156 --> 00:05:25,158
and face Lee Chung-won after that.

58
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:30,830
Then you'll be able to see
what Lee Chung-won fears the most.

59
00:05:35,918 --> 00:05:36,753
I…

60
00:05:48,222 --> 00:05:49,599
Go tell your old boss

61
00:05:50,224 --> 00:05:52,977
that you're grateful
he treated you like his own son

62
00:05:54,437 --> 00:05:56,772
and that you'll avenge him,

63
00:05:56,773 --> 00:05:58,608
no matter what it takes.

64
00:06:22,215 --> 00:06:25,885
SONS: PARK HAE-KANG, KIM GYEONG-NAM,
JANG JE-GIL, KIM DOONG-HUI

65
00:06:26,969 --> 00:06:31,766
THE APARTMENT JOB

66
00:06:36,104 --> 00:06:38,397
Why are you drinking so much?

67
00:06:40,608 --> 00:06:43,610
How many bottles have you had?
You're all drunk.

68
00:06:43,611 --> 00:06:45,195
Stop drinking!

69
00:06:45,196 --> 00:06:46,696
I'm not giving you any more.

70
00:06:46,697 --> 00:06:48,574
Just one more bottle, please.

71
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:50,534
Just one more.

72
00:06:50,535 --> 00:06:52,662
This is the last one, okay?

73
00:06:53,579 --> 00:06:54,664
Excuse me!

74
00:06:55,581 --> 00:06:58,834
The table with the bald guy.

75
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:00,253
- One bottle of soju.
- Okay.

76
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:02,671
Thank you for coming.

77
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:04,297
- Of course.
- Of course, we should come.

78
00:07:04,298 --> 00:07:06,384
- Of course.
- Tell me if you need anything.

79
00:07:09,053 --> 00:07:12,305
Big Guy, stop eating, will you?

80
00:07:12,306 --> 00:07:16,184
I'm so sad,
but I can't help feeling hungry.

81
00:07:16,185 --> 00:07:17,978
Eat as much as you want.

82
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:20,022
You sure know how to eat. Oh, hello.

83
00:07:22,817 --> 00:07:24,235
- Chew thoroughly.
- Okay.

84
00:07:44,172 --> 00:07:45,381
Mr. Park.

85
00:07:46,215 --> 00:07:49,552
Do you know who's the scariest
in a gambling den?

86
00:07:50,553 --> 00:07:52,388
The one who has nothing to lose?

87
00:07:53,639 --> 00:07:54,724
No.

88
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:59,896
It's someone
who has too many reasons not to lose.

89
00:08:03,733 --> 00:08:04,692
Look.

90
00:08:06,569 --> 00:08:08,028
All of them.

91
00:08:08,029 --> 00:08:11,657
They're the reasons you have to win.

92
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:44,565
<i>So…</i>

93
00:08:46,192 --> 00:08:48,819
<i>you have to win, no matter what it takes.</i>

94
00:08:51,113 --> 00:08:53,199
<i>That's what you have to do.</i>

95
00:09:05,503 --> 00:09:06,754
One!

96
00:09:07,838 --> 00:09:09,549
Is this a game of who talks first?

97
00:09:10,216 --> 00:09:12,926
I told you to share ideas.

98
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:16,555
We should offer a sincere apology
and promise it won't happen again--

99
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:17,472
Next.

100
00:09:17,473 --> 00:09:20,016
We should disclose
the construction process

101
00:09:20,017 --> 00:09:23,019
to restore trust
after the shoddy construction scandal--

102
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:23,979
Next.

103
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:28,484
We should promote our financial stability
to keep shareholders from pulling out…

104
00:09:31,571 --> 00:09:33,280
You know,

105
00:09:33,281 --> 00:09:36,075
you directors
are the people I envy the most.

106
00:09:36,784 --> 00:09:40,203
You get regular paychecks
even when you're so incompetent.

107
00:09:40,204 --> 00:09:43,249
What a great life.

108
00:09:46,877 --> 00:09:48,004
Listen carefully.

109
00:09:50,756 --> 00:09:54,218
Cut the prices
of the Oman New Town units in half.

110
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:58,346
Exceptional prices, premium materials,

111
00:09:58,347 --> 00:10:00,932
unlimited free safety inspections.

112
00:10:00,933 --> 00:10:03,018
Promote them aggressively,

113
00:10:03,019 --> 00:10:06,187
and get Korea's top celebrities

114
00:10:06,188 --> 00:10:09,232
to be the faces of the campaign.

115
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:10,067
But sir,

116
00:10:10,901 --> 00:10:13,029
our budget…

117
00:10:21,912 --> 00:10:23,413
Shouldn't we scrape together

118
00:10:23,414 --> 00:10:26,792
every last penny
to save our company, Director?

119
00:10:30,212 --> 00:10:31,630
What about public opinion?

120
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:36,218
The hashtag "Taesan survivor"
is still spreading on social media,

121
00:10:37,011 --> 00:10:38,678
and the legacy media

122
00:10:38,679 --> 00:10:43,475
is publishing a flood
of negative stories about Taesan.

123
00:10:43,476 --> 00:10:45,852
Social media is one thing,

124
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:48,898
but the press isn't cooperating at all.

125
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:54,194
So you mean

126
00:10:54,195 --> 00:10:57,698
the press is the problem right now.

127
00:10:58,991 --> 00:11:01,327
Please have mercy, sir!

128
00:11:08,459 --> 00:11:11,961
The Ministry of Land, Infrastructure,
and Transport is making a fuss.

129
00:11:11,962 --> 00:11:13,255
They're even talking about

130
00:11:13,839 --> 00:11:17,008
a full-scale inspection
on True Value's shoddy construction.

131
00:11:17,009 --> 00:11:20,095
It was more than
just a few cracks in the wall.

132
00:11:20,096 --> 00:11:22,806
The higher-ups are extremely unhappy

133
00:11:22,807 --> 00:11:24,974
about this scandal breaking
before the election.

134
00:11:24,975 --> 00:11:26,267
We've got a long road ahead.

135
00:11:26,268 --> 00:11:28,770
We'll all end up dead
if we keep driving with a flat tire.

136
00:11:28,771 --> 00:11:30,064
We have to replace it.

137
00:11:36,487 --> 00:11:37,571
What?

138
00:12:00,219 --> 00:12:01,595
I've picked out

139
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:04,765
your burial plots in Taegowon.

140
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:08,436
I already dug
four nice little holes for you.

141
00:12:09,145 --> 00:12:11,772
Pick the tree you want to grow there.

142
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:15,651
I thought you'd be busy,
so I brought them to you myself.

143
00:12:17,319 --> 00:12:20,655
Our Supreme Court Justice
values integrity,

144
00:12:20,656 --> 00:12:22,199
so how about a pine tree?

145
00:12:23,659 --> 00:12:26,911
And for our Senior Secretary,
who seems quite impatient,

146
00:12:26,912 --> 00:12:29,331
a plum blossom
so you'll learn perseverance.

147
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:31,541
All right.

148
00:12:31,542 --> 00:12:34,377
Pick the tree you'd like.

149
00:12:34,378 --> 00:12:36,713
What on earth are you doing?

150
00:12:36,714 --> 00:12:38,298
Arrogant bastard.

151
00:12:38,299 --> 00:12:40,718
What? "Arrogant"?

152
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:44,847
Are you deaf, or are you stupid?

153
00:12:46,015 --> 00:12:49,726
I just picked out burial plots for you.

154
00:12:49,727 --> 00:12:53,564
If you don't get your act together,
I'm going to bury you!

155
00:12:55,024 --> 00:12:57,234
The press is making quite a fuss.

156
00:12:57,985 --> 00:12:59,904
You should fix this, don't you think?

157
00:13:01,530 --> 00:13:04,407
Stop thinking about replacing the tire

158
00:13:04,408 --> 00:13:06,785
and find a way to keep the car rolling.

159
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:10,623
If I go down…

160
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:14,877
you're all going down with me.

161
00:13:19,673 --> 00:13:21,133
So please,

162
00:13:22,092 --> 00:13:24,677
keep that in mind!

163
00:13:24,678 --> 00:13:26,931
Remember that! All right?

164
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:31,852
This is

165
00:13:32,937 --> 00:13:34,146
my final warning.

166
00:13:43,405 --> 00:13:46,075
THE LATE PARK YONG-MAN

167
00:13:54,792 --> 00:13:56,377
Our old boss

168
00:13:57,127 --> 00:13:58,962
always used to come here

169
00:13:58,963 --> 00:14:01,048
after a big event.

170
00:14:02,132 --> 00:14:04,842
Even when we said
we booked a hotel buffet,

171
00:14:04,843 --> 00:14:09,430
he'd say, "Putting on belly fat
will make your punches slower!"

172
00:14:09,431 --> 00:14:12,350
But even as he said that,

173
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:15,980
he'd eat stuff like sweet and sour pork
and braised pork belly.

174
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:18,524
I miss him smacking the back of my head.

175
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:21,734
Whenever I was working alone at night,

176
00:14:21,735 --> 00:14:26,364
he'd say, "Hey, Je-gil, why are you
always working on that laptop?"

177
00:14:26,365 --> 00:14:30,201
"You'll ruin your eyes.
Keep the lights on when you're working."

178
00:14:30,202 --> 00:14:33,706
He used to tell me
I had to keep my belly full to punch well

179
00:14:34,665 --> 00:14:36,750
and that it's miserable
living on an empty stomach.

180
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:39,879
I'm so full right now,

181
00:14:40,838 --> 00:14:43,257
but I don't know why I feel so miserable.

182
00:14:58,355 --> 00:15:03,152
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR RETIREMENT

183
00:15:08,365 --> 00:15:10,658
Isn't this cape a bit much?

184
00:15:10,659 --> 00:15:12,369
- It looks good.
- It looks good.

185
00:15:13,704 --> 00:15:16,122
We already booked the hotel
and everything,

186
00:15:16,123 --> 00:15:17,665
but you just had to come here.

187
00:15:17,666 --> 00:15:18,918
Don't be silly.

188
00:15:19,585 --> 00:15:22,378
Since when did we start getting fancy
and going to hotels?

189
00:15:22,379 --> 00:15:23,631
A retirement ceremony

190
00:15:24,423 --> 00:15:27,216
should be done at a place like this,
with black bean noodles.

191
00:15:27,217 --> 00:15:29,886
Who holds a retirement ceremony
at a Chinese restaurant?

192
00:15:29,887 --> 00:15:31,347
Shut it.

193
00:15:32,222 --> 00:15:33,473
I started this job

194
00:15:33,474 --> 00:15:36,142
so I could eat
as much black bean noodles as I wanted.

195
00:15:36,143 --> 00:15:37,644
CHEERS TO YONG-MAN'S NEW BEGINNING!

196
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:40,063
And I actually did eat them
to my heart's content

197
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:42,066
working in this field all these years.

198
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:44,568
Now that I'm retired,

199
00:15:45,736 --> 00:15:48,738
I won't eat any black bean noodles again
until I'm dead.

200
00:15:48,739 --> 00:15:50,783
So congratulate me now.

201
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:53,410
I am free.

202
00:15:54,286 --> 00:15:56,163
- Congratulations!
- Congratulations!

203
00:16:01,418 --> 00:16:07,590
<i>Congratulations on your retirement</i>

204
00:16:07,591 --> 00:16:10,885
<i>Congratulations, dear Boss</i>

205
00:16:10,886 --> 00:16:13,973
<i>Congratulations on your retirement</i>

206
00:16:15,557 --> 00:16:17,476
- Congratulations!
- You punk.

207
00:16:19,186 --> 00:16:20,187
Thank you.

208
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:26,235
Now that you're retired,
can't you just live with me…

209
00:16:29,446 --> 00:16:32,282
and be my father?

210
00:16:39,957 --> 00:16:41,792
You're pretty drunk.

211
00:16:43,377 --> 00:16:44,712
I mean it.

212
00:16:46,338 --> 00:16:47,756
Park Hae-kang.

213
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:52,428
I didn't invest in you
to be treated like your father.

214
00:16:53,178 --> 00:16:56,265
You don't have to repay me.

215
00:16:58,392 --> 00:17:00,811
I'm not saying that
because I feel indebted.

216
00:17:02,021 --> 00:17:04,023
I just want to call you my father.

217
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:10,195
Don't call me your father.
It makes me cringe.

218
00:17:11,739 --> 00:17:15,491
Let's not make things harder
for each other by acting like a family.

219
00:17:15,492 --> 00:17:16,577
Got that?

220
00:17:17,911 --> 00:17:19,371
That's not fair.

221
00:17:20,039 --> 00:17:22,123
You did everything for me,

222
00:17:22,124 --> 00:17:24,959
yet you won't even let me
call you my father.

223
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:27,462
Fine, I won't do it.

224
00:17:27,463 --> 00:17:30,174
"Father"? Forget it.

225
00:17:33,469 --> 00:17:36,430
I love you, son.

226
00:17:42,644 --> 00:17:45,314
THE LATE PARK YONG-MAN

227
00:17:51,570 --> 00:17:56,532
You're the type to save people
even if you planned to do something bad.

228
00:17:56,533 --> 00:17:58,035
I know you.

229
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:09,088
You had no idea.

230
00:18:10,464 --> 00:18:12,216
I deceived you.

231
00:18:13,342 --> 00:18:14,343
But…

232
00:18:15,344 --> 00:18:17,054
I'll live my life

233
00:18:18,013 --> 00:18:19,932
proving that you were right.

234
00:18:25,854 --> 00:18:27,563
What should I do about this?

235
00:18:27,564 --> 00:18:30,858
I kept it as leverage,
as you told me to yesterday.

236
00:18:30,859 --> 00:18:33,362
We've learned that stuff like this
won't be enough.

237
00:18:34,863 --> 00:18:37,282
Get rid of it. Park Yong-man is dead too.

238
00:18:39,493 --> 00:18:41,202
But one thing I'm worried about

239
00:18:41,203 --> 00:18:43,538
is that Park Hae-kang
has nothing to lose now,

240
00:18:43,539 --> 00:18:46,083
so we don't know what he might do.

241
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:49,711
And if he finds out that
we covered up the Park Yong-man case…

242
00:18:50,295 --> 00:18:51,338
Exactly.

243
00:18:52,464 --> 00:18:55,883
Park Hae-kang and Lee Chung-won
are both crazy.

244
00:18:55,884 --> 00:18:59,679
So shouldn't we hide behind
the more powerful one in this situation?

245
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:01,932
TAESAN CONSTRUCTION LEE CHUNG-WON

246
00:19:02,766 --> 00:19:05,519
Yes, Mr. Lee. I was going to call you.

247
00:19:07,855 --> 00:19:08,814
Pardon?

248
00:19:10,232 --> 00:19:11,650
Congratulations.

249
00:19:12,901 --> 00:19:16,405
You've just become
a member of our One Club.

250
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:20,825
It's a reward for covering up
what happened with Park Yong-man.

251
00:19:20,826 --> 00:19:21,827
<i>Thank you.</i>

252
00:19:22,828 --> 00:19:26,289
We're truly on the same side now.

253
00:19:26,290 --> 00:19:27,124
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

254
00:19:27,791 --> 00:19:29,793
I'll see you at the welcome ceremony.

255
00:19:32,629 --> 00:19:34,256
We found Choi Yeong-jae, sir.

256
00:19:35,215 --> 00:19:36,216
Really?

257
00:19:36,842 --> 00:19:38,509
Where was he hiding?

258
00:19:38,510 --> 00:19:41,470
We got the security footage
around his house,

259
00:19:41,471 --> 00:19:44,515
and it seems like he was struggling
with the tenants' council president

260
00:19:44,516 --> 00:19:46,142
and got caught by Park Hae-kang's men.

261
00:19:46,143 --> 00:19:48,020
He's in the closed kindergarten now.

262
00:19:48,604 --> 00:19:50,189
We'll get him immediately.

263
00:19:51,481 --> 00:19:52,774
All right.

264
00:19:53,650 --> 00:19:56,570
What tree would suit him?

265
00:19:57,237 --> 00:19:58,529
Also,

266
00:19:58,530 --> 00:20:01,741
things seem to be getting worse
among the True Value residents.

267
00:20:01,742 --> 00:20:03,034
Park Hae-kang aside,

268
00:20:03,035 --> 00:20:07,164
the tenants' council president
keeps stirring up public opinion.

269
00:20:08,123 --> 00:20:11,210
That pageant woman again?

270
00:20:12,336 --> 00:20:14,880
Should we try giving her some money?

271
00:20:16,173 --> 00:20:18,592
Mr. Kim.

272
00:20:20,093 --> 00:20:22,094
People like that are more obsessed

273
00:20:22,095 --> 00:20:26,099
with climbing the social ladder
than money.

274
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:31,230
You've been losing your touch these days.

275
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:34,107
I'll make the preparations.

276
00:20:38,528 --> 00:20:41,531
TENANTS' COUNCIL
PRESIDENT JANG SUK-JIN

277
00:20:42,908 --> 00:20:44,325
OMAN NEW TOWN RESIDENTS' FORUM

278
00:20:44,326 --> 00:20:47,287
TAESAN'S "HALF-PRICE BARGAIN"?
HOW CAN YOU SLEEP ON A PILE OF TRASH?

279
00:20:47,871 --> 00:20:49,081
Who is it?

280
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:56,255
Wow.

281
00:20:56,755 --> 00:21:01,385
This place is completely different
from when President Seo was here.

282
00:21:02,052 --> 00:21:03,553
I'm Lee Chung-won.

283
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:08,808
I'm well aware.

284
00:21:08,809 --> 00:21:10,434
I've been posting your face

285
00:21:10,435 --> 00:21:14,146
on our online forum dozens of times a day.

286
00:21:14,147 --> 00:21:16,524
Of course I know you.

287
00:21:16,525 --> 00:21:18,360
So what brings you here?

288
00:21:21,613 --> 00:21:23,782
A penthouse in Oman New Town.

289
00:21:24,449 --> 00:21:27,703
I've set one aside just for you.

290
00:21:35,002 --> 00:21:35,877
TRUE VALUE STATE OMAN

291
00:21:36,878 --> 00:21:37,921
265-SQUARE-METER PENTHOUSE

292
00:21:38,505 --> 00:21:39,464
It's 265 square meters?

293
00:21:42,092 --> 00:21:44,969
Oh my. The view is amazing.

294
00:21:44,970 --> 00:21:49,141
It's on a whole different level
compared to our True Value.

295
00:21:49,725 --> 00:21:52,476
Why don't you stop
all this exhausting work now?

296
00:21:52,477 --> 00:21:57,357
All you have to do is say that
Taesan is providing proper compensation

297
00:21:58,025 --> 00:22:00,027
to the residents.

298
00:22:04,031 --> 00:22:05,866
But too bad.

299
00:22:06,616 --> 00:22:11,538
I want something
much more expensive than this.

300
00:22:12,914 --> 00:22:13,999
More expensive?

301
00:22:21,882 --> 00:22:25,802
The long-term repair reserve fund
that you embezzled

302
00:22:26,553 --> 00:22:30,014
and the money you siphoned off
by stuffing trash in our walls

303
00:22:30,015 --> 00:22:32,058
instead of proper materials.

304
00:22:32,059 --> 00:22:33,852
With all that combined…

305
00:22:35,896 --> 00:22:38,857
not even ten penthouses like this
would be enough.

306
00:22:39,441 --> 00:22:40,442
Don't you think?

307
00:22:41,401 --> 00:22:45,197
I graduated top of my class
from Ilhwa Women's University.

308
00:22:45,864 --> 00:22:50,535
I can tell the difference
between what's crap and what's good.

309
00:22:51,745 --> 00:22:52,746
What?

310
00:22:55,540 --> 00:22:56,583
I'm saying

311
00:22:57,918 --> 00:22:59,544
you're crap.

312
00:23:00,504 --> 00:23:01,797
So get lost, you thief.

313
00:23:04,174 --> 00:23:06,093
Don't you dare try such cheap tricks.

314
00:23:06,593 --> 00:23:08,011
Throw salt on him!

315
00:23:20,941 --> 00:23:21,942
You're beautiful.

316
00:23:25,904 --> 00:23:26,988
Gross.

317
00:23:33,120 --> 00:23:35,455
Park Hae-kang really is a mystery.

318
00:23:37,499 --> 00:23:40,168
How is everyone around him

319
00:23:40,961 --> 00:23:42,045
equally crazy?

320
00:23:50,095 --> 00:23:51,220
UNBEATABLE PRICES

321
00:23:51,221 --> 00:23:53,264
TAESAN CONSTRUCTION WILL BE REBORN

322
00:23:53,265 --> 00:23:54,724
SHOCKING PRICES FROM 10 YEARS AGO!

323
00:23:56,810 --> 00:23:58,645
Gyeong-nam, stop the car.

324
00:23:59,688 --> 00:24:00,689
Yes, Boss.

325
00:24:06,945 --> 00:24:08,155
"Reborn"?

326
00:24:08,738 --> 00:24:10,614
He's never even died before.

327
00:24:10,615 --> 00:24:12,950
Does that jerk really think
this will work?

328
00:24:12,951 --> 00:24:15,787
Everyone in Korea just saw trash
pouring out of the walls.

329
00:24:16,371 --> 00:24:18,915
Well, money makes people blind.

330
00:24:19,499 --> 00:24:22,002
And Lee Chung-won
is well aware of that fact.

331
00:24:25,255 --> 00:24:27,173
TAESAN CONSTRUCTION CONTROVERSY

332
00:24:27,174 --> 00:24:31,469
PUBLIC APOLOGY AND NEXT COURSE OF ACTION

333
00:24:47,903 --> 00:24:49,863
My fellow citizens, I am deeply sorry.

334
00:24:51,865 --> 00:24:55,534
We betrayed the valuable trust you had

335
00:24:55,535 --> 00:24:57,579
in our brand, Taesan.

336
00:24:58,163 --> 00:25:01,750
As part of our efforts
to take responsibility for this incident,

337
00:25:02,334 --> 00:25:04,336
Taesan Construction will supply

338
00:25:05,837 --> 00:25:09,215
affordable housing
through a social contribution program

339
00:25:09,216 --> 00:25:12,801
and restore the trust you've given us.

340
00:25:12,802 --> 00:25:15,179
<i>A key part of the administration's
housing supply policy,</i>

341
00:25:15,180 --> 00:25:17,389
<i>the first housing application
in the fourth new town</i>

342
00:25:17,390 --> 00:25:20,434
<i>recorded an average
competition rate of 98 to 1.</i>

343
00:25:20,435 --> 00:25:24,396
<i>Oman New Town drew strong interest
with its affordable prices</i>

344
00:25:24,397 --> 00:25:26,065
<i>and excellent location.</i>

345
00:25:26,066 --> 00:25:28,984
<i>Among them, Taesan Construction's
public housing supply</i>

346
00:25:28,985 --> 00:25:30,402
<i>for social contribution</i>

347
00:25:30,403 --> 00:25:34,031
<i>recorded an even higher competition rate
of 957 to 1.</i>

348
00:25:34,032 --> 00:25:36,575
<i>We will use this as an opportunity
to make major changes</i>

349
00:25:36,576 --> 00:25:39,453
<i>and ensure that such an incident
never happens again.</i>

350
00:25:39,454 --> 00:25:41,331
<i>We will make fundamental changes</i>

351
00:25:41,998 --> 00:25:43,333
and be reborn.

352
00:25:53,969 --> 00:25:56,178
<i>Despite the controversy
over shoddy construction,</i>

353
00:25:56,179 --> 00:26:00,349
<i>Taesan's housing program recorded
the highest-ever application rate,</i>

354
00:26:00,350 --> 00:26:03,978
<i>and Taesan Construction's stock
closed at the daily limit today.</i>

355
00:26:03,979 --> 00:26:04,979
<i>Reporter Kim Jin-su…</i>

356
00:26:04,980 --> 00:26:06,313
HIGH COMPETITION FOR OMAN NEW TOWN

357
00:26:06,314 --> 00:26:07,982
They were all barking,

358
00:26:07,983 --> 00:26:12,195
but they wag their tails
the moment I throw them a bone.

359
00:26:14,197 --> 00:26:15,657
Geez.

360
00:26:16,866 --> 00:26:18,410
TRUE VALUE STATE OMAN

361
00:26:22,455 --> 00:26:25,667
People are saying getting a Taesan
apartment is like winning the lottery.

362
00:26:26,334 --> 00:26:29,920
How can they react like that
when they know what Taesan did?

363
00:26:29,921 --> 00:26:32,423
The greed for winning the lottery

364
00:26:32,424 --> 00:26:35,509
is stronger than their fear
of shoddy construction.

365
00:26:35,510 --> 00:26:37,344
What do we do now?

366
00:26:37,345 --> 00:26:38,221
Mr. Kim.

367
00:26:40,515 --> 00:26:41,890
This won't do.

368
00:26:41,891 --> 00:26:44,686
Whether it's Taesan or Chung-won,
we'll just wipe them out.

369
00:26:45,437 --> 00:26:48,481
We're retired,
but let's go with our old methods.

370
00:26:49,149 --> 00:26:51,066
A bloody revenge for our old boss…

371
00:26:51,067 --> 00:26:52,318
I'm in.

372
00:26:52,319 --> 00:26:53,403
What's with you?

373
00:26:54,154 --> 00:26:56,156
I'll get my weapons.

374
00:27:05,457 --> 00:27:06,457
Boss.

375
00:27:06,458 --> 00:27:08,542
I'm ready to risk my life for this.

376
00:27:08,543 --> 00:27:09,793
Just give the word.

377
00:27:09,794 --> 00:27:11,211
And I'm saying this just in case,

378
00:27:11,212 --> 00:27:13,798
but don't tell us that you'll go
and fight by yourself.

379
00:27:14,632 --> 00:27:15,924
This time, we won't listen--

380
00:27:15,925 --> 00:27:17,177
Why would I?

381
00:27:20,013 --> 00:27:23,141
I have a family. Why would I fight alone?

382
00:27:24,309 --> 00:27:25,477
Family?

383
00:27:28,521 --> 00:27:29,647
Get up.

384
00:27:33,234 --> 00:27:35,027
Guys. Lizard.

385
00:27:35,028 --> 00:27:36,613
Ms. Kang Ha-ri, Kang Ha-jeong.

386
00:27:37,489 --> 00:27:38,907
Please help me

387
00:27:39,783 --> 00:27:41,409
so I can win this fight.

388
00:27:42,327 --> 00:27:43,578
I need your help.

389
00:27:44,621 --> 00:27:46,790
- He's changed.
- Boss.

390
00:27:48,249 --> 00:27:49,917
I'm a bit old,

391
00:27:49,918 --> 00:27:52,336
but I'll help in any way I can.

392
00:27:52,337 --> 00:27:53,962
I won't ask for money this time.

393
00:27:53,963 --> 00:27:55,547
I'll give you a family discount.

394
00:27:55,548 --> 00:27:57,592
I'll do anything I can to help too.

395
00:27:58,635 --> 00:27:59,928
What should we do first, Boss?

396
00:28:01,054 --> 00:28:03,306
We should start
by taking what's precious to him.

397
00:28:03,890 --> 00:28:06,767
Public opinion and the law
aren't enough to defeat him.

398
00:28:06,768 --> 00:28:09,479
We'll have to use our own method.

399
00:28:13,274 --> 00:28:14,984
So what is it?

400
00:28:38,758 --> 00:28:41,177
See? I told you they'd come.

401
00:28:43,471 --> 00:28:47,975
Mr. Choi, if you don't listen to us,
you'll really be sent to the afterlife.

402
00:28:47,976 --> 00:28:49,936
- Je-gil, go.
- Okay.

403
00:29:00,196 --> 00:29:01,823
Stop dragging that!

404
00:29:05,952 --> 00:29:06,953
What about me?

405
00:29:12,041 --> 00:29:13,752
Was this really our best option?

406
00:29:15,003 --> 00:29:18,006
We have another mouth to feed now.
Our living expenses…

407
00:29:23,803 --> 00:29:25,221
How long have you been the manager?

408
00:29:26,514 --> 00:29:28,307
Do you want to lose this hand?

409
00:29:28,308 --> 00:29:31,185
All my joints are aching

410
00:29:31,186 --> 00:29:33,979
from staying trapped in the kindergarten.

411
00:29:33,980 --> 00:29:37,025
How did you know
this stuff is good for your joints?

412
00:29:37,609 --> 00:29:40,277
This is supposed to be good
for sore knees, right?

413
00:29:40,278 --> 00:29:42,154
It's good for stiff shoulders too.

414
00:29:42,155 --> 00:29:44,990
I had six pills for each meal,
and it was really effective.

415
00:29:44,991 --> 00:29:47,242
Geez. No wonder
they disappeared so quickly.

416
00:29:47,243 --> 00:29:50,454
Don't you know what they say
about overusing medicine?

417
00:29:50,455 --> 00:29:52,122
The recommended amount is two pills!

418
00:29:52,123 --> 00:29:54,334
He doesn't know what that means.

419
00:29:55,084 --> 00:29:57,629
Mr. Choi, have it with water.

420
00:29:58,213 --> 00:29:59,838
Thanks, Ha-jeong.

421
00:29:59,839 --> 00:30:02,049
Are you seriously accepting that?

422
00:30:02,050 --> 00:30:05,552
Did you forget how you framed
my sister and Mr. Park for embezzlement?

423
00:30:05,553 --> 00:30:07,387
You little…

424
00:30:07,388 --> 00:30:08,431
Well…

425
00:30:09,265 --> 00:30:11,350
I only did as Mr. Lee ordered.

426
00:30:11,351 --> 00:30:13,977
Taegowon isn't just a tree farm, is it?

427
00:30:13,978 --> 00:30:15,062
Where's the money?

428
00:30:15,063 --> 00:30:17,397
I don't know that either.

429
00:30:17,398 --> 00:30:18,483
But…

430
00:30:19,317 --> 00:30:21,401
whenever we took money out of the fund,

431
00:30:21,402 --> 00:30:23,862
we delivered it to Taegowon.

432
00:30:23,863 --> 00:30:25,281
Me and President Seo.

433
00:30:25,865 --> 00:30:28,784
In any case, all the money
embezzled from apartment complexes

434
00:30:28,785 --> 00:30:30,495
must all be there somewhere.

435
00:30:32,038 --> 00:30:34,748
Then our 17.8 billion should be there too.

436
00:30:34,749 --> 00:30:36,376
That 17.8 billion.

437
00:30:37,001 --> 00:30:38,085
Should we steal it back?

438
00:30:38,086 --> 00:30:39,754
- Of course.
- Sounds good.

439
00:30:40,463 --> 00:30:43,799
Yes. Lee Chung-won
values that more than his life.

440
00:30:43,800 --> 00:30:45,759
Let's take these

441
00:30:45,760 --> 00:30:48,345
and strip him bare.

442
00:30:48,346 --> 00:30:49,347
Yes, Boss.

443
00:30:50,181 --> 00:30:51,266
All right.

444
00:31:06,698 --> 00:31:08,825
You lost Choi Yeong-jae again?

445
00:31:09,701 --> 00:31:10,743
Mr. Kim.

446
00:31:11,452 --> 00:31:12,287
No…

447
00:31:17,417 --> 00:31:18,418
Eun-ho.

448
00:31:19,085 --> 00:31:21,671
You weren't like this before.

449
00:31:22,797 --> 00:31:24,215
I'm sorry, sir.

450
00:31:25,258 --> 00:31:28,636
When we were swinging steel pipes
at demolition sites,

451
00:31:29,596 --> 00:31:33,266
you were full of ruthless determination.

452
00:31:33,933 --> 00:31:35,143
We came

453
00:31:36,269 --> 00:31:38,479
all the way here with that determination.

454
00:31:40,398 --> 00:31:41,524
I'm sorry, sir.

455
00:31:42,483 --> 00:31:45,361
There's no point
in looking decent on the outside…

456
00:31:48,197 --> 00:31:49,157
if this…

457
00:31:51,701 --> 00:31:52,744
this…

458
00:31:55,747 --> 00:31:56,831
and this…

459
00:31:58,291 --> 00:32:00,418
have all lost that determination.

460
00:32:11,596 --> 00:32:14,390
Park Hae-kang
even took Choi Yeong-jae now.

461
00:32:15,600 --> 00:32:18,019
I'm so jealous.

462
00:32:20,146 --> 00:32:22,190
What will his next step be?

463
00:32:23,483 --> 00:32:24,692
I'm so curious.

464
00:32:47,256 --> 00:32:50,258
Look at this.
It's practically a fortress, not a farm.

465
00:32:50,259 --> 00:32:52,552
They've got infrared sensors
set up everywhere,

466
00:32:52,553 --> 00:32:56,264
and their guards aren't hired muscle.
They're security consulting professionals.

467
00:32:56,265 --> 00:32:58,225
So we can't face them head-on.

468
00:32:58,226 --> 00:33:00,227
And it's not like
we can fly in like drones.

469
00:33:00,228 --> 00:33:01,687
Do we have to dig through?

470
00:33:01,688 --> 00:33:03,730
- Then I'll go get shovels.
- Hey.

471
00:33:03,731 --> 00:33:05,942
He was just saying that.
Do you take him for a fool?

472
00:33:08,194 --> 00:33:09,612
If we can't go inside…

473
00:33:12,657 --> 00:33:14,283
we can make them come out.

474
00:33:15,827 --> 00:33:17,452
Is this the district office?

475
00:33:17,453 --> 00:33:19,871
I'd like to report
illegally dumped waste from Taegowon.

476
00:33:19,872 --> 00:33:20,998
Illegal dumping!

477
00:33:20,999 --> 00:33:24,001
Hello, I'm a reporter
from <i>Gongyeong Daily.</i>

478
00:33:24,002 --> 00:33:25,753
Are there any plans
to investigate Taegowon?

479
00:33:26,421 --> 00:33:29,756
There's a stench of rotten meat
coming from Taegowon.

480
00:33:29,757 --> 00:33:31,842
I'm sure there's some
illegal butchering going on.

481
00:33:31,843 --> 00:33:34,554
Shouldn't you be doing
an emergency health inspection?

482
00:33:38,558 --> 00:33:39,766
Is this the district office?

483
00:33:39,767 --> 00:33:42,477
Yes, I'm hearing screaming every night
coming from Taegowon.

484
00:33:42,478 --> 00:33:44,814
They must be burying people in there.

485
00:33:46,774 --> 00:33:48,650
I'm a former guard from there.

486
00:33:48,651 --> 00:33:51,361
They have a dog farm in their basement.

487
00:33:51,362 --> 00:33:53,613
They even hunt and eat protected animals.

488
00:33:53,614 --> 00:33:55,115
If you don't believe me, go and…

489
00:33:55,116 --> 00:33:56,700
Is this the inspection office?

490
00:33:56,701 --> 00:34:01,330
I'd like to report the Environmental
Department for neglecting their duties…

491
00:34:02,165 --> 00:34:03,915
If you don't crack down on them now,

492
00:34:03,916 --> 00:34:06,294
we'll consider it collusion
and report it to the press.

493
00:34:09,505 --> 00:34:10,422
ENVIRONMENTAL DEPARTMENT

494
00:34:10,423 --> 00:34:13,550
Leachate? That's a tree farm, though.

495
00:34:13,551 --> 00:34:15,928
A party with drugs?
Then you should call the police…

496
00:34:16,512 --> 00:34:19,056
What? Dereliction of duty?

497
00:34:19,057 --> 00:34:20,223
An audit?

498
00:34:20,224 --> 00:34:21,933
Why would you audit our… Hello?

499
00:34:21,934 --> 00:34:25,312
Hey! What the hell
is this fuss about Taegowon?

500
00:34:25,313 --> 00:34:27,355
We're getting reports on illegal dumping,

501
00:34:27,356 --> 00:34:29,649
illegal drug use,
and that it's a drug den.

502
00:34:29,650 --> 00:34:31,818
Even environmental groups
received the reports.

503
00:34:31,819 --> 00:34:34,905
If we don't send someone,
the website will crash from complaints.

504
00:34:34,906 --> 00:34:38,034
Hey, gather a team
and go check Taegowon immediately!

505
00:34:46,542 --> 00:34:49,879
Mr. Lee, do we have to trim these today?

506
00:34:50,588 --> 00:34:51,713
The thing about trees

507
00:34:51,714 --> 00:34:55,258
is that they have to be frightened
for them to take a beautiful shape.

508
00:34:55,259 --> 00:34:59,638
So it's the perfect time to shape them,
just like you.

509
00:34:59,639 --> 00:35:01,849
Was threatening us
at the hotel not enough?

510
00:35:03,768 --> 00:35:07,187
I'm just saying
you won't have to get your hands dirty.

511
00:35:07,188 --> 00:35:11,776
I just got a useful tool
that can take care of all the hard work.

512
00:35:19,659 --> 00:35:21,702
It's nice to see you, sirs.

513
00:35:25,998 --> 00:35:27,082
I'm Kwak Ju-gwon.

514
00:35:27,083 --> 00:35:31,712
Together with all of you,
I'll properly prune this country.

515
00:35:33,005 --> 00:35:35,215
Did you get the ten billion?

516
00:35:35,216 --> 00:35:38,219
Or did you two make
some kind of deal behind our backs?

517
00:35:38,803 --> 00:35:42,848
Taesan has been in hot water lately
because of the shoddy construction.

518
00:35:42,849 --> 00:35:45,685
You're going to have to become
our shield, Commissioner.

519
00:35:46,394 --> 00:35:47,644
Don't worry.

520
00:35:47,645 --> 00:35:50,438
My specialty is paving the road ahead

521
00:35:50,439 --> 00:35:53,151
so you won't have to deal
with any dust flying around.

522
00:35:53,651 --> 00:35:54,860
You heard that, right?

523
00:35:54,861 --> 00:35:58,405
Our new member is great
at taking care of the cleanup.

524
00:35:58,406 --> 00:36:00,740
So don't worry about a flat tire.

525
00:36:00,741 --> 00:36:04,912
Commissioner Kwak is going to have
the entire road blocked off.

526
00:36:05,496 --> 00:36:06,497
Round of applause.

527
00:36:11,627 --> 00:36:13,087
OFFICIAL DUTY

528
00:36:15,715 --> 00:36:17,424
Hello.

529
00:36:17,425 --> 00:36:18,633
What is this about?

530
00:36:18,634 --> 00:36:20,844
- We're from the district office.
- The district office?

531
00:36:20,845 --> 00:36:22,262
They came by this morning.

532
00:36:22,263 --> 00:36:24,014
We're from the department above them.

533
00:36:24,015 --> 00:36:25,140
The department above them?

534
00:36:25,141 --> 00:36:26,850
This is a serious matter.

535
00:36:26,851 --> 00:36:28,768
With everything going on,

536
00:36:28,769 --> 00:36:31,521
we have no choice
but to conduct a thorough investigation.

537
00:36:31,522 --> 00:36:33,398
What more are you trying to investigate?

538
00:36:33,399 --> 00:36:35,483
What on earth are you doing in here?

539
00:36:35,484 --> 00:36:36,443
What are you doing?

540
00:36:36,444 --> 00:36:37,903
This isn't a tree farm, is it?

541
00:36:37,904 --> 00:36:39,237
- We already know.
- Calm down.

542
00:36:39,238 --> 00:36:40,322
We're getting complaints!

543
00:36:40,323 --> 00:36:41,781
The higher-ups are throwing a fit!

544
00:36:41,782 --> 00:36:43,618
- I wish I could tell you--
- Enough!

545
00:36:44,744 --> 00:36:46,745
We came here first
because it'll get out of hand

546
00:36:46,746 --> 00:36:47,954
if the police come too.

547
00:36:47,955 --> 00:36:49,706
So please understand.

548
00:36:49,707 --> 00:36:51,625
There are guests present.

549
00:36:51,626 --> 00:36:53,210
Please return tomorrow morning.

550
00:36:53,211 --> 00:36:55,045
This makes it seem more suspicious.

551
00:36:55,046 --> 00:36:56,796
Mr. Jang, call the cops.

552
00:36:56,797 --> 00:36:58,298
We'll come back with the police.

553
00:36:58,299 --> 00:37:00,342
Why are they complicating things?

554
00:37:00,343 --> 00:37:01,594
Wait!

555
00:37:02,470 --> 00:37:04,179
It's fine. We'll come with the police.

556
00:37:04,180 --> 00:37:05,138
Right.

557
00:37:05,139 --> 00:37:06,015
Wait…

558
00:37:07,516 --> 00:37:09,351
Please make it fast.

559
00:37:09,352 --> 00:37:10,685
- Shall we?
- Sure.

560
00:37:10,686 --> 00:37:11,770
- Shall we?
- Make it quick?

561
00:37:11,771 --> 00:37:13,313
- Then check thoroughly.
- Okay.

562
00:37:13,314 --> 00:37:16,025
We have to report this to our chief,
so take photos too. Let's go.

563
00:37:16,609 --> 00:37:18,735
We're not some random weirdos.

564
00:37:18,736 --> 00:37:21,739
You shouldn't interfere
with government duties.

565
00:37:24,492 --> 00:37:25,867
- Don't look back.
- What is it?

566
00:37:25,868 --> 00:37:26,826
They're following us.

567
00:37:26,827 --> 00:37:28,287
Keep looking forward. Act natural.

568
00:37:35,544 --> 00:37:36,587
You're all gathered here.

569
00:37:37,421 --> 00:37:39,464
What kind of performance is this?

570
00:37:39,465 --> 00:37:41,549
- Only authorized personnel…
- Sure.

571
00:37:41,550 --> 00:37:43,970
Supreme Court Justice,
Senior Secretary for Civil Affairs,

572
00:37:44,971 --> 00:37:47,390
Prosecutor General,
President of <i>Gongyeong Daily,</i>

573
00:37:48,015 --> 00:37:49,141
and…

574
00:37:49,976 --> 00:37:52,310
our new member, Commissioner Kwak.

575
00:37:52,311 --> 00:37:55,022
After all that fuss, you finally got in.

576
00:37:56,691 --> 00:37:58,359
The One Club sure is something.

577
00:37:59,360 --> 00:38:02,028
You're Korea's most powerful figures,

578
00:38:02,029 --> 00:38:05,740
and you're just sitting here
trimming trees?

579
00:38:05,741 --> 00:38:07,952
Mr. Lee, what are you doing? Kick him out.

580
00:38:08,536 --> 00:38:09,620
Park Hae-kang.

581
00:38:10,705 --> 00:38:13,290
Do you have a death wish?

582
00:38:13,291 --> 00:38:16,376
Taegowon. <i>Tae,</i> meaning big.
<i>Go,</i> meaning high.

583
00:38:16,377 --> 00:38:19,170
For a place with such a lofty name,

584
00:38:19,171 --> 00:38:21,756
what lies beneath is pretty rotten.

585
00:38:21,757 --> 00:38:24,051
How dare you speak that way
in front of us?

586
00:38:25,136 --> 00:38:27,470
I have something to show you.

587
00:38:27,471 --> 00:38:29,514
I took some photos on the way,

588
00:38:29,515 --> 00:38:32,350
and they have such pretty nameplates
for every tree.

589
00:38:32,351 --> 00:38:34,269
They're called memorial trees.

590
00:38:34,270 --> 00:38:37,272
This one's name is Kim Hong-hyeon.

591
00:38:37,273 --> 00:38:38,690
Taesan's finance team leader

592
00:38:38,691 --> 00:38:40,901
who supposedly fled overseas
five years ago.

593
00:38:41,736 --> 00:38:43,653
And this tree's name is Lee Jae-gu.

594
00:38:43,654 --> 00:38:47,283
Assemblyman Lee Jae-gu,
who went missing three years ago.

595
00:38:48,242 --> 00:38:49,909
And this one is

596
00:38:49,910 --> 00:38:51,536
Nam Hui-jae.

597
00:38:51,537 --> 00:38:54,040
Oh, right.
That's the newspaper company president.

598
00:38:54,582 --> 00:38:55,833
Shut up.

599
00:38:59,712 --> 00:39:01,129
And there was also a tree

600
00:39:01,130 --> 00:39:03,591
with the name of our former
residents' association president.

601
00:39:06,635 --> 00:39:07,720
Should I try digging?

602
00:39:12,141 --> 00:39:13,934
Or should I leave them be?

603
00:39:14,852 --> 00:39:17,813
Shut up, you bastard.

604
00:39:21,525 --> 00:39:22,902
You'd better hurry.

605
00:39:23,694 --> 00:39:26,446
Things that stink
should be cleaned quickly.

606
00:39:26,447 --> 00:39:27,281
Wouldn't you agree?

607
00:39:28,824 --> 00:39:30,993
I'll get going, then.

608
00:39:32,703 --> 00:39:33,704
Have a good day.

609
00:39:54,100 --> 00:39:57,435
Sir, it seems like
the elders have noticed.

610
00:39:57,436 --> 00:39:58,686
Don't worry.

611
00:39:58,687 --> 00:40:01,315
Those geezers
won't be able to say anything.

612
00:40:03,651 --> 00:40:05,778
Park Hae-kang was throwing bait.

613
00:40:06,946 --> 00:40:09,198
He'll be waiting for us to dig them up.

614
00:40:10,199 --> 00:40:12,118
Then what should we do, sir?

615
00:40:13,994 --> 00:40:17,206
We'll dig…

616
00:40:19,542 --> 00:40:20,960
just as he wants.

617
00:40:22,002 --> 00:40:23,128
We'll begin right away.

618
00:40:23,129 --> 00:40:25,004
Use rented trucks,

619
00:40:25,005 --> 00:40:27,465
and change all the license plates.

620
00:40:27,466 --> 00:40:30,636
Move everything,
and don't leave a speck of dirt behind.

621
00:40:31,303 --> 00:40:34,306
But Taesan's warehouse will be too risky.

622
00:40:38,477 --> 00:40:39,562
I know a place.

623
00:40:40,729 --> 00:40:42,481
Somewhere no one can even imagine.

624
00:41:03,669 --> 00:41:05,962
It's cramped. Stop pushing.

625
00:41:05,963 --> 00:41:09,299
We don't know when it'll be over,
so have at least two sandwiches.

626
00:41:09,300 --> 00:41:10,801
You're on your fourth one.

627
00:41:11,760 --> 00:41:13,094
Well, it's so good.

628
00:41:13,095 --> 00:41:14,305
You're right about that.

629
00:41:16,098 --> 00:41:17,308
They're coming out.

630
00:41:18,309 --> 00:41:19,642
They're coming out.

631
00:41:19,643 --> 00:41:21,812
Stay on your targets, everyone.

632
00:41:28,360 --> 00:41:30,028
That's going in the opposite direction.

633
00:41:30,029 --> 00:41:31,697
We're going that way.

634
00:41:42,500 --> 00:41:44,627
Team 1, turning left.

635
00:41:45,961 --> 00:41:48,087
My heart's about to burst.

636
00:41:48,088 --> 00:41:50,174
It's way more nerve-racking
than in the movies.

637
00:41:53,135 --> 00:41:56,262
Whatever's in that truck
is what we're after, right?

638
00:41:56,263 --> 00:42:00,475
Yes. President Park made the call,
so we should trust him.

639
00:42:00,476 --> 00:42:03,269
I think we just got caught
by a speed camera.

640
00:42:03,270 --> 00:42:05,814
My makeup's all cakey, though.
Should I touch up my lipstick?

641
00:42:08,275 --> 00:42:10,318
Team 2, turning right.

642
00:42:10,319 --> 00:42:11,986
Hold on tight.

643
00:42:11,987 --> 00:42:14,657
Step on it.
Let's crush them for good today.

644
00:42:18,911 --> 00:42:20,995
This must be the real deal.

645
00:42:20,996 --> 00:42:22,914
They must've noticed. They're speeding up.

646
00:42:22,915 --> 00:42:24,959
Mr. Kim seems to be pretty anxious.

647
00:42:28,212 --> 00:42:29,505
Stick closer to him.

648
00:43:04,248 --> 00:43:05,207
He's gone.

649
00:43:06,041 --> 00:43:07,876
- He left.
- Let's go.

650
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:20,681
He's not coming out.

651
00:43:21,265 --> 00:43:23,601
He's just leaving the truck out here?

652
00:43:24,810 --> 00:43:25,935
Let's go.

653
00:43:25,936 --> 00:43:27,396
This is too easy.

654
00:43:28,731 --> 00:43:30,816
- Big Guy, keep an eye out.
- Okay.

655
00:43:36,697 --> 00:43:37,948
Open it.

656
00:43:41,201 --> 00:43:42,328
Oops.

657
00:43:43,746 --> 00:43:45,330
- What is this?
- Boss!

658
00:43:45,331 --> 00:43:46,165
What's going on?

659
00:43:53,422 --> 00:43:54,798
What's going on?

660
00:43:55,924 --> 00:43:57,009
It's a trap!

661
00:43:59,762 --> 00:44:01,721
- Are you ready?
- For what?

662
00:44:01,722 --> 00:44:02,681
Run!

663
00:44:19,031 --> 00:44:21,033
- Let's lead them to the rooftop!
- Yes, Boss!

664
00:44:39,176 --> 00:44:40,469
Hang in there. Don't let go.

665
00:44:47,017 --> 00:44:48,352
Now! Run!

666
00:45:56,086 --> 00:45:57,754
- Is your stomach okay?
- No, it hurts.

667
00:46:02,926 --> 00:46:04,094
Mr. Park! Get in!

668
00:46:05,095 --> 00:46:06,346
Lizard!

669
00:46:09,391 --> 00:46:11,226
- Park Hae-kang!
- No!

670
00:46:20,444 --> 00:46:21,528
Lizard.

671
00:46:26,992 --> 00:46:27,868
Lizard.

672
00:46:30,412 --> 00:46:32,413
- He got stabbed.
- Where?

673
00:46:32,414 --> 00:46:33,373
Where?

674
00:46:35,334 --> 00:46:36,626
Gyeong-nam, get in!

675
00:46:36,627 --> 00:46:38,294
- Je-gil!
- We need an ambulance!

676
00:46:38,295 --> 00:46:39,253
Open your eyes!

677
00:46:39,254 --> 00:46:40,297
- Lizard!
- Open your eyes!

678
00:46:44,051 --> 00:46:45,427
Go!

679
00:46:48,972 --> 00:46:51,183
You idiots! Go after them!

680
00:46:54,895 --> 00:46:56,729
- Mr. Park…
- You're okay.

681
00:46:56,730 --> 00:46:58,649
Breathe. Stay with me.

682
00:47:05,113 --> 00:47:07,324
Stay with me, Lizard.

683
00:47:07,824 --> 00:47:09,867
We're going to the hospital.
Hang in there.

684
00:47:09,868 --> 00:47:10,911
They used a knife?

685
00:47:12,246 --> 00:47:13,829
Am I bleeding a lot?

686
00:47:13,830 --> 00:47:16,624
Wait. Hold on. Blood…

687
00:47:16,625 --> 00:47:18,627
He's not bleeding.

688
00:47:19,127 --> 00:47:20,878
Can't you even tell? Look carefully.

689
00:47:20,879 --> 00:47:23,005
He really isn't bleeding.

690
00:47:23,006 --> 00:47:23,966
Lizard!

691
00:47:32,349 --> 00:47:34,141
I'm really thorough, you know.

692
00:47:34,142 --> 00:47:36,186
The car is so fancy,
the manual is thick as hell.

693
00:47:36,979 --> 00:47:38,813
Geez! You scared us to death!

694
00:47:38,814 --> 00:47:40,064
God, that scared me.

695
00:47:40,065 --> 00:47:41,024
What the heck?

696
00:47:42,859 --> 00:47:44,610
I'm a bit touched, though.

697
00:47:44,611 --> 00:47:47,196
I thought handsome guys like you
would be cold-blooded.

698
00:47:47,197 --> 00:47:50,241
"Lizard! Open your eyes!"

699
00:47:50,242 --> 00:47:52,743
"We're going to the hospital!
Stay with me! Open your eyes!"

700
00:47:52,744 --> 00:47:53,828
"Hang in there, Lizard!"

701
00:47:53,829 --> 00:47:55,497
"Keep breathing!"

702
00:47:56,081 --> 00:47:57,790
Hey, Lizard.

703
00:47:57,791 --> 00:47:59,542
Do you want to visit the rooftop again?

704
00:47:59,543 --> 00:48:01,127
I'm sorry… "Lizard!"

705
00:48:01,128 --> 00:48:03,379
"Open your eyes!
We're going to the hospital!"

706
00:48:03,380 --> 00:48:05,006
- "Stay with me, Lizard!"
- Geez.

707
00:48:05,007 --> 00:48:06,132
"Lizard!"

708
00:48:06,133 --> 00:48:08,385
We should go to the nearest rooftop, Boss.

709
00:48:16,643 --> 00:48:17,894
Should we

710
00:48:18,937 --> 00:48:20,439
head back now?

711
00:48:21,440 --> 00:48:23,899
Let's head back to our apartment complex.

712
00:48:23,900 --> 00:48:25,235
Not yet.

713
00:48:25,819 --> 00:48:26,944
Why not?

714
00:48:26,945 --> 00:48:30,282
No more trucks are coming out.
We've been waiting for a long time.

715
00:48:31,742 --> 00:48:33,243
<i>Ms. Kang Ha-ri, you wait at the gate.</i>

716
00:48:34,077 --> 00:48:35,703
If the other trucks are fake,

717
00:48:35,704 --> 00:48:38,414
the real one could come out last,
looking the least suspicious.

718
00:48:38,415 --> 00:48:40,250
If that's the case, follow that car.

719
00:48:52,179 --> 00:48:54,681
That one! It's the real one
Mr. Park was talking about!

720
00:48:56,600 --> 00:48:57,893
Goodness.

721
00:49:05,359 --> 00:49:06,901
Lee Chung-won!

722
00:49:06,902 --> 00:49:08,320
You saw that sly fox, right?

723
00:49:25,128 --> 00:49:26,213
Hey.

724
00:49:27,089 --> 00:49:30,050
Isn't this the way to True Value?

725
00:49:30,926 --> 00:49:33,511
All the other trucks were just bait.

726
00:49:33,512 --> 00:49:35,347
The real one was going to True Value.

727
00:49:36,348 --> 00:49:37,557
Oh my gosh.

728
00:49:54,866 --> 00:49:56,325
He's going in.

729
00:49:56,326 --> 00:49:57,828
He's entering the parking lot.

730
00:50:05,752 --> 00:50:06,919
DO NOT ENTER

731
00:50:06,920 --> 00:50:08,714
- Lower the window.
- What is this?

732
00:50:09,715 --> 00:50:12,133
Sir! Is there no one here?

733
00:50:12,134 --> 00:50:13,509
- Sir!
- I don't see anyone.

734
00:50:13,510 --> 00:50:15,762
- Hang on. I can't see.
- Darn it. We have to hurry.

735
00:50:17,764 --> 00:50:19,473
- Call them.
- Excuse me!

736
00:50:19,474 --> 00:50:21,100
Anyone there?

737
00:50:21,101 --> 00:50:22,269
Sir!

738
00:50:23,186 --> 00:50:24,520
So you mean

739
00:50:24,521 --> 00:50:27,857
the money went to one
of the 9,800 households?

740
00:50:27,858 --> 00:50:29,943
The odds are 1 in 9,800.

741
00:50:30,861 --> 00:50:32,361
That's too broad.

742
00:50:32,362 --> 00:50:35,698
The money came back
to our apartment complex.

743
00:50:35,699 --> 00:50:39,076
We'll find it even if we have
to press 9,800 doorbells.

744
00:50:39,077 --> 00:50:41,580
We don't have to look
through 9,800 households.

745
00:50:42,080 --> 00:50:44,541
We just have to find the one house

746
00:50:45,125 --> 00:50:48,128
that Lee Chung-won chose among them.

747
00:51:02,726 --> 00:51:04,685
What about Park Hae-kang?

748
00:51:04,686 --> 00:51:06,103
It's fine.

749
00:51:06,104 --> 00:51:09,356
Killing Park Hae-kang
wasn't our goal today.

750
00:51:09,357 --> 00:51:11,651
Our goal was to distract him.

751
00:51:12,986 --> 00:51:14,987
And the car in the parking lot?

752
00:51:14,988 --> 00:51:16,198
He won't be able to find it.

753
00:51:28,502 --> 00:51:29,878
This is so good.

754
00:51:41,932 --> 00:51:42,766
Nice.

755
00:51:51,650 --> 00:51:52,692
Damn it.

756
00:51:53,819 --> 00:51:55,361
I thought Lee Chung-won

757
00:51:55,362 --> 00:51:57,363
was our incinerator

758
00:51:57,364 --> 00:52:01,033
who cleaned up our messes
without leaving a trace.

759
00:52:01,034 --> 00:52:02,451
I did too.

760
00:52:02,452 --> 00:52:04,495
But he didn't get rid of our waste.

761
00:52:04,496 --> 00:52:07,582
He was collecting it
and even putting name tags on it.

762
00:52:10,585 --> 00:52:12,504
Let's get Hanmin to take over.

763
00:52:13,797 --> 00:52:15,006
All right.

764
00:52:18,552 --> 00:52:21,554
Sorry I'm late.
Your call was quite sudden…

765
00:52:21,555 --> 00:52:22,931
Commissioner.

766
00:52:24,140 --> 00:52:25,642
- Hello.
- Please sit.

767
00:52:29,813 --> 00:52:32,982
Commissioner, I'm curious about something.

768
00:52:32,983 --> 00:52:36,151
What do the police usually do
if a car accident

769
00:52:36,152 --> 00:52:38,655
causes a huge traffic jam?

770
00:52:39,406 --> 00:52:40,407
Pardon?

771
00:52:43,827 --> 00:52:46,412
We have the vehicles towed
and clear the scene quickly.

772
00:52:46,413 --> 00:52:48,497
That's right. You tow them.

773
00:52:48,498 --> 00:52:52,418
Lee Chung-won is like a truck
in a car accident right now.

774
00:52:52,419 --> 00:52:56,256
The control system's down,
and the body is huge,

775
00:52:57,257 --> 00:52:58,800
so it's completely blocking our path.

776
00:53:01,052 --> 00:53:02,261
What?

777
00:53:02,262 --> 00:53:04,264
You can tow him away,

778
00:53:05,390 --> 00:53:06,808
can't you?

779
00:53:18,069 --> 00:53:19,321
I understand.

780
00:53:20,113 --> 00:53:21,323
I'll follow protocol

781
00:53:22,282 --> 00:53:23,909
and take care of it quietly.

782
00:53:27,037 --> 00:53:28,997
Yes. Follow protocol.

783
00:53:32,500 --> 00:53:33,835
- Je-gil.
- Yes?

784
00:53:35,170 --> 00:53:36,171
No, wait.

785
00:53:40,634 --> 00:53:43,178
- You can see all the residents.
- Yes.

786
00:53:46,681 --> 00:53:48,098
Did you order something again?

787
00:53:48,099 --> 00:53:49,934
You need to eat to stay strong.

788
00:53:49,935 --> 00:53:52,811
I was feeling a bit down,
so I made some pancakes.

789
00:53:52,812 --> 00:53:57,066
Mr. Choi, I made
your favorite kimchi pancakes.

790
00:53:57,067 --> 00:53:58,985
- Thank you.
- Hello, President Jang.

791
00:54:00,820 --> 00:54:01,655
Oh my gosh.

792
00:54:02,405 --> 00:54:04,908
Ms. Kang, how are you here?

793
00:54:05,659 --> 00:54:07,285
Hello.

794
00:54:08,578 --> 00:54:12,916
You were hiding her here
and didn't tell me anything?

795
00:54:13,500 --> 00:54:16,586
We weren't hiding her.
We just thought she'd be the safest here.

796
00:54:17,253 --> 00:54:18,338
Oh my.

797
00:54:18,964 --> 00:54:21,048
I can't believe it.

798
00:54:21,049 --> 00:54:24,469
All of you are gathered here.

799
00:54:26,388 --> 00:54:29,640
I didn't even know you two were sisters.

800
00:54:29,641 --> 00:54:31,726
Looking at you now, you do look alike.

801
00:54:32,394 --> 00:54:35,980
But Ms. Kang,
you seem to have lost so much weight.

802
00:54:35,981 --> 00:54:37,356
Eat up.

803
00:54:37,357 --> 00:54:38,524
Thank you.

804
00:54:38,525 --> 00:54:43,362
But we have to find Lee Chung-won's vault
among 9,800 houses.

805
00:54:43,363 --> 00:54:44,905
Where could he have hidden it?

806
00:54:44,906 --> 00:54:46,240
The community center?

807
00:54:46,241 --> 00:54:48,659
Or some kind of storage room
we don't know about?

808
00:54:48,660 --> 00:54:49,536
Mr. Choi.

809
00:54:50,537 --> 00:54:53,205
There are too many people
visiting the community center,

810
00:54:53,206 --> 00:54:57,710
and the cleaning ladies
use the storage room several times a day.

811
00:54:57,711 --> 00:54:59,295
- He wouldn't use that.
- Hang on.

812
00:54:59,963 --> 00:55:01,880
Then wouldn't he hide it in his own house?

813
00:55:01,881 --> 00:55:05,426
The penthouse would be huge.

814
00:55:05,427 --> 00:55:08,595
But he'll get busted
as soon as a search warrant is issued.

815
00:55:08,596 --> 00:55:09,805
Then Mr. Choi.

816
00:55:09,806 --> 00:55:11,056
Yes, sir?

817
00:55:11,057 --> 00:55:13,267
There's no need to get up.

818
00:55:13,268 --> 00:55:15,728
You're making it look like
I'm really rude.

819
00:55:15,729 --> 00:55:16,688
Sorry, sir.

820
00:55:17,981 --> 00:55:22,484
Then doesn't Lee Chung-won
own any other units in True Value?

821
00:55:22,485 --> 00:55:23,945
Even under a different name?

822
00:55:26,698 --> 00:55:29,992
There aren't any on the list of owners.

823
00:55:29,993 --> 00:55:32,077
Then what about under Mr. Kim's name?

824
00:55:32,078 --> 00:55:33,997
There's no need.

825
00:55:34,831 --> 00:55:37,083
How about units
that were recently vacated?

826
00:55:37,751 --> 00:55:38,917
Even if they're not,

827
00:55:38,918 --> 00:55:42,297
units with unusually low
electricity or water usage.

828
00:55:42,881 --> 00:55:44,632
Can you check units like that?

829
00:55:45,925 --> 00:55:48,427
I know this unit. Unit 105.

830
00:55:48,428 --> 00:55:51,055
Their kids went to study abroad.

831
00:55:51,056 --> 00:55:52,848
That's why they're not home.

832
00:55:52,849 --> 00:55:55,768
And Building 307, Unit 1802.

833
00:55:55,769 --> 00:55:58,020
Gosh, Mr. Choi. Remember?

834
00:55:58,021 --> 00:56:02,066
They caused a huge scene
after the man cheated on his wife.

835
00:56:02,067 --> 00:56:03,484
The man left first,

836
00:56:03,485 --> 00:56:05,444
but the woman
doesn't come home these days.

837
00:56:05,445 --> 00:56:08,655
So they're both having an affair.
What about the kids?

838
00:56:08,656 --> 00:56:10,199
Then there are three houses left.

839
00:56:10,200 --> 00:56:11,658
If there are only three left,

840
00:56:11,659 --> 00:56:14,661
can't we just break into them
and check for ourselves?

841
00:56:14,662 --> 00:56:18,791
Hey, they're owned units.
You could get sued for breaking in.

842
00:56:18,792 --> 00:56:21,419
Wait. There's one more unit.

843
00:56:22,170 --> 00:56:24,963
The maintenance fee
is being paid automatically,

844
00:56:24,964 --> 00:56:27,592
but there hasn't been
any water usage the past month.

845
00:56:28,593 --> 00:56:29,844
Where is it?

846
00:56:31,930 --> 00:56:33,973
Unit 2903. Seo Gang-won's house.

847
00:56:50,448 --> 00:56:52,617
I got it in one go. Come on.

848
00:56:56,162 --> 00:56:58,497
Hey, Gyeong-nam.

849
00:56:58,498 --> 00:56:59,790
You actually got the passcode?

850
00:56:59,791 --> 00:57:01,708
- Be quiet.
- That's amazing.

851
00:57:01,709 --> 00:57:03,211
There's no one here.

852
00:57:06,131 --> 00:57:07,507
What is all that?

853
00:57:08,883 --> 00:57:10,009
This is crazy!

854
00:57:12,762 --> 00:57:13,887
What? Is this all cash?

855
00:57:13,888 --> 00:57:15,807
All of this is cash?

856
00:57:16,641 --> 00:57:18,100
This…

857
00:57:18,101 --> 00:57:18,935
No way!

858
00:57:21,020 --> 00:57:22,147
It's cash.

859
00:57:22,689 --> 00:57:24,107
We found Lee Chung-won's vault.

860
00:57:25,108 --> 00:57:26,900
I've never seen

861
00:57:26,901 --> 00:57:29,486
so much cash before in my life.

862
00:57:29,487 --> 00:57:31,780
He really does things
on a different scale.

863
00:57:31,781 --> 00:57:33,907
He sure is bold.

864
00:57:33,908 --> 00:57:36,118
But this seems to be
more than 17.8 billion.

865
00:57:36,119 --> 00:57:37,035
Really?

866
00:57:37,036 --> 00:57:40,372
He embezzled funds
from other apartment complexes too.

867
00:57:40,373 --> 00:57:42,708
He used it all as his personal fund.

868
00:57:42,709 --> 00:57:43,792
Oh my gosh.

869
00:57:43,793 --> 00:57:45,669
Then we…

870
00:57:45,670 --> 00:57:47,713
What do we do

871
00:57:47,714 --> 00:57:49,090
about all this money?

872
00:57:49,799 --> 00:57:51,967
We'll take our 17.8 billion

873
00:57:51,968 --> 00:57:54,471
and return the rest
to the other apartment complexes.

874
00:57:58,975 --> 00:58:00,268
What's with you?

875
00:58:00,935 --> 00:58:04,229
We need something
to stake our claim to this money.

876
00:58:04,230 --> 00:58:07,024
We should report it first, right?

877
00:58:07,025 --> 00:58:09,610
We need to take care of this legally.

878
00:58:09,611 --> 00:58:11,069
No.

879
00:58:11,070 --> 00:58:13,655
Lee Chung-won has connections
in the police too. It won't work.

880
00:58:13,656 --> 00:58:15,657
We might end up losing the money again.

881
00:58:15,658 --> 00:58:18,827
Lee Chung-won's name
isn't in the ledger my sister wrote.

882
00:58:18,828 --> 00:58:20,954
He'll easily get away with this.

883
00:58:20,955 --> 00:58:22,999
We'll lose if we go by the law.

884
00:58:24,626 --> 00:58:27,629
Then we can use this situation
to our advantage.

885
00:58:29,005 --> 00:58:30,131
How?

886
00:58:32,592 --> 00:58:34,760
Mr. Choi and Ms. Kang Ha-jeong
can take the blame.

887
00:58:34,761 --> 00:58:35,803
What?

888
00:58:36,596 --> 00:58:38,723
Right. That's a good idea.

889
00:58:39,599 --> 00:58:41,518
This is President Seo's house.

890
00:58:42,101 --> 00:58:43,143
You can say

891
00:58:43,144 --> 00:58:47,231
that the money you embezzled is here
and that you felt guilty,

892
00:58:47,232 --> 00:58:49,859
so you'd like to return
all the money you pocketed.

893
00:58:50,735 --> 00:58:53,195
Like a public confession?

894
00:58:53,196 --> 00:58:55,447
You should brace yourself.

895
00:58:55,448 --> 00:58:56,573
My gosh.

896
00:58:56,574 --> 00:58:58,742
Lee Chung-won
won't be able to claim that it's his.

897
00:58:58,743 --> 00:59:00,702
If he does, he'll become an embezzler

898
00:59:00,703 --> 00:59:03,122
and have to explain
President Seo's disappearance.

899
00:59:04,040 --> 00:59:05,123
Bravo.

900
00:59:05,124 --> 00:59:06,583
That's such a good idea.

901
00:59:06,584 --> 00:59:08,627
You're so smart.

902
00:59:08,628 --> 00:59:12,673
Let's reveal the 17.8 billion
to the residents first.

903
00:59:12,674 --> 00:59:14,258
We'll make the announcement

904
00:59:14,259 --> 00:59:17,135
that President Park
got our reserve fund back.

905
00:59:17,136 --> 00:59:19,180
- What do you think?
- That's good.

906
00:59:19,973 --> 00:59:24,352
We'll make all 9,800 households
our witnesses.

907
00:59:27,021 --> 00:59:31,692
I'm going to turn myself in
after we reveal the money tomorrow,

908
00:59:31,693 --> 00:59:33,069
as I promised.

909
00:59:34,320 --> 00:59:35,822
Don't be too scared.

910
00:59:39,075 --> 00:59:42,160
Thank you for everything so far.

911
00:59:42,161 --> 00:59:43,288
For protecting me.

912
00:59:45,623 --> 00:59:47,666
Once you're released,

913
00:59:47,667 --> 00:59:51,420
I'll be waiting with a cake,

914
00:59:51,421 --> 00:59:52,839
so hurry back.

915
00:59:54,799 --> 00:59:56,426
Cake? Not tofu?

916
00:59:57,385 --> 01:00:00,012
Well, I…

917
01:00:00,013 --> 01:00:02,598
I didn't trust women
after what happened with my ex-wife.

918
01:00:02,599 --> 01:00:06,101
But you're like an angel.

919
01:00:06,102 --> 01:00:09,813
I learned that
there are kind people like you too.

920
01:00:09,814 --> 01:00:12,441
I heard that you want
to become a patissier.

921
01:00:12,442 --> 01:00:15,611
So I thought you'd like it
if I got a cake for you instead.

922
01:00:15,612 --> 01:00:18,364
Well, I was just trying to flirt.

923
01:00:23,453 --> 01:00:26,205
I like mango cakes.

924
01:00:28,708 --> 01:00:29,709
Mango…

925
01:00:37,634 --> 01:00:39,843
"Hands in the air.
I'll shoot if you move."

926
01:00:39,844 --> 01:00:42,471
But then the woman raised her head,

927
01:00:42,472 --> 01:00:44,514
and her eyes weren't human.

928
01:00:44,515 --> 01:00:45,933
Isn't that scary?

929
01:00:48,269 --> 01:00:49,187
Hey.

930
01:00:51,064 --> 01:00:52,939
What's wrong, Big Guy?

931
01:00:52,940 --> 01:00:53,941
Big Guy.

932
01:00:57,737 --> 01:00:58,696
I'm cold!

933
01:01:00,448 --> 01:01:01,491
What's with you?

934
01:01:06,287 --> 01:01:07,121
Drink.

935
01:01:09,540 --> 01:01:13,252
You still have to face the consequences.

936
01:01:14,003 --> 01:01:16,672
But you've been very cooperative,

937
01:01:16,673 --> 01:01:20,550
so we'll submit petitions for leniency

938
01:01:20,551 --> 01:01:22,345
on your behalf.

939
01:01:24,931 --> 01:01:25,932
Thank you…

940
01:01:26,641 --> 01:01:27,558
so much.

941
01:01:29,519 --> 01:01:30,561
Drink up.

942
01:01:37,527 --> 01:01:39,069
Get some sleep.

943
01:01:39,070 --> 01:01:41,072
You look like your eyes
are about to pop out.

944
01:01:42,115 --> 01:01:43,449
I'm not sleepy.

945
01:01:45,743 --> 01:01:48,371
You need your strength for tomorrow.

946
01:01:48,913 --> 01:01:50,789
Want to lean on my shoulder?

947
01:01:50,790 --> 01:01:51,624
Here.

948
01:01:54,669 --> 01:01:55,795
Really?

949
01:02:02,301 --> 01:02:03,469
Gosh.

950
01:02:04,887 --> 01:02:08,223
You can end your date and head inside now.
I'll keep watch.

951
01:02:08,224 --> 01:02:09,850
- It's not like that!
- We weren't!

952
01:02:09,851 --> 01:02:12,060
Why are you yelling?

953
01:02:12,061 --> 01:02:14,647
I didn't see anything.

954
01:02:15,940 --> 01:02:17,400
We didn't do anything.

955
01:02:18,067 --> 01:02:20,862
You were all…

956
01:02:21,904 --> 01:02:22,739
What?

957
01:02:25,283 --> 01:02:27,201
What's wrong with you?

958
01:02:31,247 --> 01:02:33,166
Everything will be over tomorrow, right?

959
01:02:34,459 --> 01:02:38,086
I'm so excited to see
the look on Lee Chung-won's face.

960
01:02:38,087 --> 01:02:41,549
We have to make sure
he'll never be able to smile again.

961
01:02:42,216 --> 01:02:43,342
Never.

962
01:02:45,595 --> 01:02:48,638
And after everything's
wrapped up tomorrow,

963
01:02:48,639 --> 01:02:50,850
you should get back
to studying for the bar exam.

964
01:02:51,601 --> 01:02:53,519
I'll help you in your sister's place.

965
01:02:54,812 --> 01:02:56,230
We're family.

966
01:03:03,362 --> 01:03:04,280
Why?

967
01:03:06,908 --> 01:03:08,576
Why would you go that far?

968
01:03:09,827 --> 01:03:10,661
Can't you…

969
01:03:12,371 --> 01:03:14,457
just think of me as Daddy-Long-Legs?

970
01:03:15,416 --> 01:03:16,583
What?

971
01:03:16,584 --> 01:03:17,460
No way.

972
01:03:18,628 --> 01:03:19,836
What?

973
01:03:19,837 --> 01:03:23,048
That line was a bit cringe, you know.

974
01:03:23,049 --> 01:03:24,091
What do you mean?

975
01:03:25,051 --> 01:03:27,344
Daddy-Long-Legs is a good thing.

976
01:03:27,345 --> 01:03:29,513
- It's like a benefactor.
- Mr. Park.

977
01:03:29,514 --> 01:03:32,098
Don't you know the ending
of <i>Daddy-Long-Legs?</i>

978
01:03:32,099 --> 01:03:35,603
Judy Abbott ends up marrying
that Daddy-Long-Legs.

979
01:03:36,312 --> 01:03:37,396
They get married?

980
01:03:39,565 --> 01:03:43,778
Are you saying you'll make me
into Judy Abbott and try something funny?

981
01:03:44,529 --> 01:03:46,696
You're a scary man.

982
01:03:46,697 --> 01:03:47,739
I…

983
01:03:47,740 --> 01:03:49,407
That's not what I meant.

984
01:03:49,408 --> 01:03:51,744
Judy actually… Geez.

985
01:03:52,328 --> 01:03:53,913
This is bad, Ms. Kang!

986
01:03:55,289 --> 01:03:59,377
WE FOUND THE LOST 17.8 BILLION!

987
01:04:08,052 --> 01:04:09,470
I didn't know money was so heavy.

988
01:04:10,847 --> 01:04:13,224
Great job!

989
01:04:19,105 --> 01:04:22,608
All right, President Park.
You should say something.

990
01:04:23,317 --> 01:04:26,403
We couldn't have found it
without President Park.

991
01:04:26,404 --> 01:04:27,654
He's amazing.

992
01:04:27,655 --> 01:04:28,572
Right.

993
01:04:28,573 --> 01:04:31,324
I knew President Park
would be able to resolve this elegantly.

994
01:04:31,325 --> 01:04:34,452
Then we all helped
find the reserve fund, didn't we?

995
01:04:34,453 --> 01:04:36,246
- Of course!
- We did it together.

996
01:04:36,247 --> 01:04:39,541
Everyone, I'm at the True Value site.

997
01:04:39,542 --> 01:04:41,793
Do you see those apple boxes?

998
01:04:41,794 --> 01:04:44,672
They're actually filled with cash.
The real fund.

999
01:04:48,843 --> 01:04:51,470
Hello. I'm President Park Hae-kang.

1000
01:04:54,557 --> 01:04:57,810
The reason why I asked you all
to gather here today

1001
01:04:58,603 --> 01:05:01,062
is that our facility manager
and accounting manager

1002
01:05:01,063 --> 01:05:03,607
decided to reveal
the location of the lost fund,

1003
01:05:03,608 --> 01:05:06,027
and we've brought it all back.

1004
01:05:09,030 --> 01:05:12,115
What's more, I wanted you all
to see the money in person

1005
01:05:12,116 --> 01:05:14,159
to prevent unnecessary misunderstandings.

1006
01:05:14,160 --> 01:05:15,076
Goodness.

1007
01:05:15,077 --> 01:05:18,163
I'd like you to check our reserve fund
with your own eyes

1008
01:05:18,164 --> 01:05:21,583
and keep showing your interest
in True Value's matters

1009
01:05:21,584 --> 01:05:23,877
so this will never happen again.

1010
01:05:23,878 --> 01:05:26,672
We'd like for every one of you
to be watchdogs of the community.

1011
01:05:28,549 --> 01:05:34,346
- Watchdogs!
- Watchdogs!

1012
01:05:34,347 --> 01:05:36,766
- Watchdogs!
- Hey, come down.

1013
01:05:37,600 --> 01:05:39,184
All right, everyone.

1014
01:05:39,185 --> 01:05:41,353
I will now show you
True Value's reserve fund

1015
01:05:41,354 --> 01:05:44,523
that we've gotten back
with your sacrifice and cooperation.

1016
01:05:54,283 --> 01:05:56,327
All right. Here is your reserve…

1017
01:05:57,328 --> 01:05:58,536
- Hurry up!
- What's he doing?

1018
01:05:58,537 --> 01:06:00,206
Come on!

1019
01:06:01,123 --> 01:06:02,750
- What's he doing?
- What is it?

1020
01:06:09,048 --> 01:06:10,382
What is it?

1021
01:06:10,383 --> 01:06:12,593
Stop messing around and show us.

1022
01:06:18,140 --> 01:06:19,517
- What?
- What is that?

1023
01:06:26,357 --> 01:06:28,109
What's going on?

1024
01:06:34,699 --> 01:06:37,326
LIZARD

1025
01:06:38,327 --> 01:06:41,163
<i>Mr. Park, did you forget
that I'm the Lizard?</i>

1026
01:06:41,914 --> 01:06:45,166
<i>Cutting off a tail is nothing to me.</i>

1027
01:06:45,167 --> 01:06:47,920
<i>I'll take the money.</i>

1028
01:06:57,179 --> 01:06:58,722
Open the other boxes.

1029
01:06:58,723 --> 01:07:00,390
Open the one next to it!

1030
01:07:00,391 --> 01:07:01,850
That one too?

1031
01:07:01,851 --> 01:07:03,727
What? What's going on?

1032
01:07:03,728 --> 01:07:04,562
What's this?

1033
01:07:05,604 --> 01:07:06,772
What is all this?

1034
01:07:13,571 --> 01:07:15,656
I'm sure the money was in here.

1035
01:07:30,546 --> 01:07:31,714
We got robbed again?

1036
01:07:45,061 --> 01:07:52,026
Lizard!

1037
01:07:58,115 --> 01:08:01,035
THE APARTMENT JOB

1038
01:08:37,696 --> 01:08:39,698
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park
